# The age SECRET key that decrypts every submission ever sent. Never commit it
# -- not even to a private repo: history is permanent and access can widen
# later. Keep it in a password manager with an offsite copy. Losing it makes
# every encrypted package undecryptable forever, which has already happened
# once (commit 93e5de7 in the desktop repo).
